{"nodes": [{"id": "agents", "label": "AGENTS.md \u2014 NeuroONE Agent Operating Contract", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_plan_mode", "label": "PLAN Mode", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "PLAN is the default operating mode because 'a correct implementation of the wrong architecture is still a failure'. Heavy architectural reasoning is front-loaded so another capable engineer could implement without rediscovering the architecture.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_build_mode", "label": "BUILD Mode", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "BUILD is execution, not architectural improvisation; surfacing an unresolved design decision mid-implementation forces a return to PLAN rather than an ad-hoc call.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_debug_mode", "label": "DEBUG Mode", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Evidence-driven defect resolution with the smallest safe change. Identify the layer where the contract FIRST becomes incorrect, not where the error surfaced, so symptom is never mistaken for root cause.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_test_mode", "label": "TEST Mode", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A passing happy path is not sufficient evidence of correctness; verdict must be one of PASS / PASS WITH KNOWN LIMITATIONS / FAIL / BLOCKED, and production behavior is never changed merely to satisfy an incorrect test.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_mode_transitions", "label": "Mode Transition State Machine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a711", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_document_precedence", "label": "Source-of-Truth Precedence", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "PRD > APP-FLOW > TRD > MVP-SCOPE. MVP-SCOPE is the current decision layer that narrows/sequences but cannot widen scope past PRD \u00a77. Conflicts are never silently resolved \u2014 name the conflict, return to PLAN, recommend a resolution.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.1, \u00a73.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_clinical_safety_boundary", "label": "Clinical Safety Boundary (non-negotiable)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "NeuroONE assists clinicians and must never be built or presented as autonomous diagnosis, a replacement for clinician judgment, or automated treatment. The USP narrative about early detection is vision language wrapping a clinician-assist tool \u2014 product copy must not migrate into product behavior.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_mvp_demo_purpose", "label": "MVP as Investor/Stakeholder Demo", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The bar is 'demonstrates the full product concept convincingly end-to-end', not production clinical deployment. This relaxes rigor for AI/RAG implementation depth ONLY \u2014 never for security, layer boundaries, typed contracts, the safety boundary, or data integrity.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_architecture_rules", "label": "Layered Architecture Rules (Client \u2192 API \u2192 Service \u2192 Repository \u2192 PostgreSQL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_transaction_boundary_ownership", "label": "Open Convention \u2014 Transaction Boundary Ownership", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "TRD.md does not assign transaction-boundary ownership between repository and service. It must be picked once in an ADR before the first multi-repository use case, rather than settled implicitly per-endpoint.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_overridable_service_providers", "label": "Overridable Auth Service Providers", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Authentication dependencies expose overridable service providers instead of constructing services inside request dependencies, so the auth path stays testable.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_ai_failure_safety", "label": "AI/RAG Failure Safety Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An AI or RAG failure must never corrupt or partially overwrite a patient or clinical case record: preserve clinical data, return a controlled error, allow retry/recovery.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a78.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_ai_output_contract", "label": "Extended AI Output Contract (Diagnosis with category and trend_basis)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a78.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_never_definitive_diagnosis", "label": "Never Represent Output as Definitive Diagnosis", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "FR-04 constraint applied everywhere \u2014 not in the schema, not in API field naming, not in UI copy, not in the PDF. Confidence is always expressed as likelihood, never as certainty.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a78.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_security_privacy_rules", "label": "Security and Privacy Rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a712", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_error_handling_rules", "label": "Centralized Error Handling Rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a713", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_task_planning_format", "label": "Task Planning Format", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a714", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_repository_inspection_rules", "label": "Repository Inspection Rules", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Documentation describes intent; the repository describes reality, and on this project the two have already diverged (the Visit model is a known stub). Never plan from docs alone when the task depends on current implementation state.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a716", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_decision_records", "label": "Decision Record (ADR) Policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a717", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_definition_of_done", "label": "Agent Definition of Done Checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a718", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_v1_scope_guard", "label": "V1 Scope Guard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_clinical_input_contract", "label": "Structured Clinical Input Contract", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Symptoms, duration, severity, observations and history are validated at the schema boundary and must not collapse into a free-text blob, because the AI pipeline's normalization and cross-visit trend comparison depend on their structure.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_report_contract", "label": "Report Completeness Contract", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A report missing citations or the disclaimer is incomplete, not merely unpolished.", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "agents", "target": "docs_prd", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents", "target": "docs_app_flow", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents", "target": "docs_trd", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents", "target": "docs_neuroone_mvp_scope", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_document_precedence", "target": "docs_prd", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_